UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Master Mind Scholarship at KU Leuven', provider = 'Flemish Ministry of Education and Training (via KU Leuven)', coverage_type = 'Full Funding', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'For 2027-2028 entry: applications opened 15 October 2026 and close 15 January 2027, 23.59 CET - submit the complete master''s application (with the KU Leuven Scholarships & Master Mind Candidacy Form as an annexe) and register the scholarship candidacy online, both by the deadline; nominees are informed by 10 March 2027.', deadline_date = '2027-01-15', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Eligible English-taught KU Leuven master's programmes (per the published 2027-2028 eligible-programmes list; bridging and distance-learning programmes are excluded)"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Master Mind Scholarship is the Flemish Ministry of Education and Training's flagship award for outstanding international students coming to Flanders and Brussels for a master's degree; this record is the KU Leuven route into it. For 2027-2028, Master Mind holders at KU Leuven receive a grant of €10,750 - published by KU Leuven as covering the full length of the programme, in line with the per-academic-year grant of previous cycles (€10,225 in 2026-2027) - alongside tuition charged at approximately the EEA tariff (about €1,200 per academic year, i.e. without the non-EEA surcharge); tenure is one academic year for a 60-ECTS master's and two academic years for a 120-ECTS master's, and KU Leuven lists three scholarships for this cycle, with the information expressly preliminary and subject to confirmation no later than January 2027. One application process covers several awards at once: Master Mind applicants are automatically also considered for KU Leuven's Inspiring the Outstanding Scholarship and - where nationality matches - the KU Leuven ASEAN, Africa and Central and South America scholarships. The route is nomination-based at Flemish level: applicants file a complete master's application including the KU Leuven Scholarships & Master Mind Candidacy Form and register their candidacy online by 15 January 2027 (23.59 CET); nominees hear by 10 March 2027 and submit a one-minute motivational video by 16 March 2027, with selection results at the end of March. The scholarships are highly competitive and are assessed on academic performance and awards, motivation, relevant experience, leadership and commitment.$desc$, requirements = $req$All nationalities are eligible. Applicants must show a high standard of academic performance and potential, reflected in a high GPA on the transcript of records, and previous degree(s) must have been obtained at a higher-education institution outside Flanders (credit mobility at a Flemish host does not disqualify). Students already enrolled at a Flemish higher-education institution are not eligible (except those in a specific preparatory programme ahead of a September 2027 master's start), and the award cannot be combined with any other scholarship from KU Leuven, the Belgian national or regional governments, or the European Commission. Bridging and distance-learning programmes are excluded; the master's must be on KU Leuven's eligible-programmes list. English: regardless of the programme's own minimum, non-native speakers must demonstrate a good command of English (test taken before the 15 January deadline, results may follow) - KU Leuven's general minima are IELTS 6.5 overall (Academic) or TOEFL iBT 79, while the previous Master Mind cycle set the scholarship bar at IELTS 7.0 / TOEFL 94; confirm the 2027-2028 figure when final terms are published (by January 2027). No numeric GPA cutoff is published and the scholarship-level English score is not fixed for this cycle, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://www.kuleuven.be/scholarships/year/2027-2028/master-mind-scholarship', source_url = 'https://www.kuleuven.be/scholarships/year/2027-2028/master-mind-scholarship', application_url = 'https://www.kuleuven.be/english/apply', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'open', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 108) from KU Leuven's official 'The Master Mind Scholarship' 2027-2028 page and English Proficiency Tests page, both fetched the same day (sponsor: Flemish Ministry of Education and Training; grant of €10,750 'to cover the full length of their programme'; tuition at approximately the EEA tariff of €1,200/year rather than the non-EEA rate; duration one year for a 60-ECTS master and two years for a 120-ECTS master; three scholarships listed for this cycle; applications 15 October 2026 to 15 January 2027 23.59 CET; candidacy-form annexe + online registration, nomination by 10 March 2027, one-minute video by 16 March, results end of March; all nationalities eligible; prior degree outside Flanders; no combination with KU Leuven/Belgian/EC scholarships; automatic consideration for Inspiring the Outstanding and the regional KU Leuven scholarships). Reliability 9 (not 10) because KU Leuven flags the 2027-2028 information as 'preliminary and subject to change, pending confirmation no later than January 2027', and the €10,750 phrasing (kept verbatim in the description) does not repeat the explicit 'per academic year' wording of the 2026-2027 page (€10,225 per academic year, full tuition waiver) - the annual-grant reading matches the Master Mind series and sibling records 411/785, and award is stored as a fixed €10,750/year on that basis. The previously stored website URL pointed to a different scheme (the Faculty of Science's Science@Leuven Scholarship) and is corrected; this record joins the existing Master Mind family (411 central Flemish record, 581 Ghent, 785 VUB) as the KU Leuven instance. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (qualitative high-GPA standard; scholarship-level English score not fixed for 2027-2028 - last cycle IELTS 7.0/TOEFL 94 vs KU Leuven general IELTS 6.5/TOEFL 79, recorded in text). university_scholarships row 46 synced; source 2559 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official scheme page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read.$note$, award_amount = 10750, award_currency = 'EUR', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'fixed', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Grant of €10,750 (per academic year, per the Master Mind series; KU Leuven states it covers the full programme length) + tuition at the EEA tariff (approx. €1,200/year); 3 scholarships at KU Leuven for 2027-2028 (terms preliminary pending January 2027 confirmation)', tuition_coverage = 'Holders pay tuition at approximately the EEA tariff (~€1,200 per academic year); the non-EEA surcharge is waived, so this is a reduced-fee package rather than a full tuition waiver for 2027-2028 (preliminary terms).', english_requirements = 'Good command of English regardless of programme minimum (test before 15 January; results may follow). KU Leuven general minima: IELTS 6.5 overall / TOEFL iBT 79; the 2026-2027 Master Mind cycle required IELTS 7.0 / TOEFL 94 - confirm the 2027-2028 figure on the official page.', required_documents = $j$["Complete application file for an eligible KU Leuven master's by 15 January 2027, 23.59 CET, including the KU Leuven Scholarships & Master Mind Candidacy Form uploaded as document type 'Annexe'", "Registration of the scholarship candidacy via KU Leuven's online registration tool by the same deadline", "English proficiency test taken before the deadline (results may be added afterwards)", "If nominated: one-minute motivational video by 16 March 2027"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"cycle": "2027-2028 entry", "opens": "2026-10-15", "deadline": "2027-01-15", "nomination_notice": "2027-03-10", "status": "open"}, {"pattern": "Annual: applications open mid-October and close 15 January (23.59 CET) for the following academic year; nominees informed by 10 March, results end of March"}]$json$ WHERE id = 144;

UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 108) after official-source review: the Ghent University Top-up Grants for master's students from OESO-DAC-list countries (formerly a €1,000/month allowance plus all-in insurance, with tuition at the EEA rate, awarded by nomination) no longer exists as a live, verifiable scheme on Ghent University's official website. The previously stored URL (ugent.be/en/research/funding/bof/topup-grants.htm) returns 404; the former scheme and overview pages under the Global South section are likewise gone, and the university's current 'Scholarship possibilities for candidates from the Global South' page (fetched 2026-10-27, which previously headlined 'Top-up Grants (Masters)') now lists only VLIRUOS ICP Connect (restricted to 29 eligible countries), IFS research backpacks and a link to the separate BOF Doctoral Scholarships for candidates from the Global South. Every remaining description of the Top-up Grants is a secondary aggregator copy of a withdrawn UGent page, so re-verifying the scheme first-hand is impossible and presenting it as a live award would repeat the aggregators' stale claim. The stored title also conflated the master's Top-up Grants with Special Research Fund (BOF) doctoral fellowships, a different instrument, so the composite record is retired rather than rewritten into either half; UGent's BOF Doctoral Scholarships for the Global South can be assessed for the catalogue separately on their official terms (they require an eligible UGent promoter and typically co-financing). Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 623 withdrawn; source 2647 repointed to the current official Global South scholarship-possibilities page.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 410;

UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 108) after official-source review: no Vrije Universiteit Brussel scheme named 'VUB International Master Scholarship' exists. The previously stored URL (vub.be financial-support scholarships page) returns 404, and VUB's current official scholarship-programmes listing (checked 2026-10-27) offers named instruments instead - the Flemish Government's Master Mind scholarship (already catalogued for VUB as record 785, with the central record 411), Erasmus Mundus scholarships (e.g. 4CITIES Urban Studies), the VUB Scholarships for the MSc in Photonics Engineering, VLIR-UOS ICP Master scholarships, PRONABEC and China Scholarship Council routes, and smaller programme-level grants. An invented umbrella name over that portfolio is a directory entry, not a scholarship an applicant can apply for, and rewriting it into one of the unrelated named schemes would violate the cleanup's identity rule, so the record is retired. Individual live schemes (e.g. the Photonics scholarships) can be added later only as separately verified records in an additions batch. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. Source 2694 repointed to VUB's current official scholarships listing.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 412;

UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-27 (cleanup pass 108) after official-source review: no 'UCLouvain International Excellence Scholarship' exists at UCLouvain. The previously stored URL was the enrolment portal (uclouvain.be/en/study/inscriptions), not a scholarship page, and UCLouvain's official international-student FAQ states plainly: 'UCLouvain does not grant scholarships to international bachelor's or master's students' - funding is directed instead to outside bodies (ARES-CCD, DGD, AUF, Erasmus Mundus and home-country sources). The record's pan-level title (Bachelor's/Master's/PhD) is an invented umbrella over financial-aid topography (social-rate tuition reductions, external funders and exchange/mobility grants), so it is retired rather than rewritten into an unrelated instrument. One genuinely new scheme was noticed in passing - the Louvain School of Engineering's (EPL) Excellence Scholarships covering full tuition for international master's students in engineering, computer science and data science - which is a faculty-level award distinct from this record and is noted as a candidate for a later additions batch after first-hand verification. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 498 withdrawn; source 832 repointed to the official UCLouvain FAQ page carrying the no-scholarships statement.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 479;

UPDATE sources SET url = CASE id WHEN 2559 THEN 'https://www.kuleuven.be/scholarships/year/2027-2028/master-mind-scholarship' WHEN 2647 THEN 'https://www.ugent.be/en/research/funding/globalsouth/globalsouth-grants.htm' WHEN 2694 THEN 'https://www.vub.be/en/scholarships' WHEN 832 THEN 'https://uclouvain.be/en/international/bachelor-master-faq' ELSE url END, title = CASE id WHEN 2559 THEN 'The Master Mind Scholarship 2027-2028 - KU Leuven (official)' WHEN 2647 THEN 'Scholarship possibilities for candidates from the Global South - Ghent University (official)' WHEN 2694 THEN 'Scholarships - Vrije Universiteit Brussel (official listing)' WHEN 832 THEN 'International student FAQ - UCLouvain (official)' ELSE title END, domain = CASE id WHEN 2559 THEN 'kuleuven.be' WHEN 2647 THEN 'ugent.be' WHEN 2694 THEN 'vub.be' WHEN 832 THEN 'uclouvain.be' ELSE domain END, source_type = 'official_page', accessed_at = now(), is_official = true, is_verified = true WHERE id IN (832, 2559, 2647, 2694);

UPDATE university_scholarships SET scholarship_name = CASE id WHEN 46 THEN 'Master Mind Scholarship at KU Leuven' WHEN 623 THEN 'Ghent University Top-Up Grants (retired: scheme withdrawn from the official site; composite title)' WHEN 498 THEN 'UCLouvain International Excellence Scholarship (retired: no such award)' ELSE scholarship_name END, availability_status = CASE WHEN id IN (498, 623) THEN 'No' ELSE 'available' END, funding_type = CASE id WHEN 46 THEN 'Master Mind grant + reduced (EEA-tariff) tuition' WHEN 623 THEN 'Retired (2026-10-27)' WHEN 498 THEN 'Retired (2026-10-27)' ELSE funding_type END, max_scholarship = CASE id WHEN 46 THEN '€10,750 grant + tuition at the EEA tariff (approx. €1,200/year) for 2027-2028 (preliminary terms)' WHEN 623 THEN 'No live award of this name: UGent has withdrawn the Top-up Grants pages from its official site' WHEN 498 THEN 'No such award: UCLouvain states it does not grant scholarships to international bachelor''s or master''s students' ELSE max_scholarship END, covers_tuition = CASE WHEN id = 46 THEN true ELSE covers_tuition END, covers_living_expenses = CASE WHEN id = 46 THEN true ELSE covers_living_expenses END, official_url = CASE WHEN id = 46 THEN 'https://www.kuleuven.be/scholarships/year/2027-2028/master-mind-scholarship' ELSE official_url END, source_url = CASE WHEN id = 46 THEN 'https://www.kuleuven.be/scholarships/year/2027-2028/master-mind-scholarship' ELSE source_url END, verification_status = CASE WHEN id IN (498, 623) THEN 'withdrawn' ELSE 'verified' END, last_verified_at = now() WHERE id IN (46, 498, 623);
